      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #59212.\n\nInstead of keeping the last 9 chars, keep IDs that are already valid and hash the others to 9 base62 chars. Calls and results get the same mapping, and it's stable across turns. Also removes the per-call warning (#58647).\n\nNot duplicating anything: #47739 is about generated IDs for `tool_choice=\"required\"`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```\npytest tests/tokenizers_/test_mistral.py tests/renderers/test_mistral.py tests/parser/mistral\npytest tests/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/test_serving_chat.py -k mistral\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\nNew tests (v3 + v13 tokenizers, long/short/non-alphanumeric/shared-suffix IDs): 6/9 fail on main, all pass with this PR. Existing suites pass, ruff clean.\n\nWritten with help from Claude Code; I reviewed it and ran the tests.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\n</details>\n",
